MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8de559a088a5d4d48bb00ae8ccc21165, type: 3}
  m_Name: Predator Hunting Season
  crisisName: Predator Hunting Season
  ominousWarningText: "Fresh tracks have begun appearing around the settlement, larger and more numerous than the hunters remember seeing before. Game that once wandered close to camp has retreated deeper into the wilderness, and even experienced hunters return with little to show for days spent beyond the fires. At night, unfamiliar cries echo through the trees, sometimes answered by others from far across the valley. A few hunters insist that the predators are simply following migrating prey, but others have noticed tracks circling shelters and food stores before disappearing back into the darkness. Fires are being kept burning longer, and fewer people now venture out alone. For the first time in many seasons, the hunters are beginning to wonder whether they are still the ones doing the hunting."
  obviousWarningText: "The predators no longer hide their presence. Their calls can be heard just beyond the light of the fires, and shadowy forms have been spotted moving between the trees after sunset. Packs that once hunted separately now travel together along familiar hunting trails and near the approaches to the settlement. Scouts report that several animals have begun ignoring ordinary attempts to frighten them away, as though hunger or competition has overcome their fear of people. Hunting parties are returning early, and families have begun bringing children and livestock closer to the center of camp. Whatever has driven so many predators into our territory, they are no longer merely passing through. They are gathering."
  crisisStartText: "The hunt has changed. Predators are pouring into our territory in numbers rarely seen before, following dwindling prey ever closer to human settlements. Packs stalk familiar trails, large hunters linger near camps, and the wilderness itself has become more dangerous to cross. Predator populations will remain unusually high while the crisis lasts, threatening hunters, travelers, and isolated units. Our people can answer by hunting the beasts, strengthening their numbers, or simply surviving until the balance of nature returns. For now, every journey beyond the fires carries new risk."
  ominousWarningTurns: 1
  obviousWarningTurns: 1
  durationTurns: 6
  useAgeWindow: 1
